    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Judiciary",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6561\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act in relation to terms and conditions of employment of certain\nnonjudicial officers and employees of the unified court system\n\nThis measure is being introduced at the request of the Judiciary. It\nimplements a collective bargaining agreement between the State and a\npublic employee union (CSEA) negotiating on behalf of court employees\nin the State Judiciary collective negotiating unit. This collective\nbargaining agreement provides salary increases and other benefits for\nthe period from April 1, 2017 through March 31, 2020.\n\nThere are approximately 5,500 employees in the State Judiciary\ncollective negotiating unit. They serve in courts in all areas of the\nState, from western New York to the eastern tip of Long Island, from\nthe north country by the Canadian border to the southern tier.\n\n-Provides for the payment of pensionable annual longevity payments,\neffective April 1, 2017, April 1, 2018 and April 1, 2019, and on April\n1 of each fiscal year thereafter, to graded employees who have\ncompleted at least four years of continuous service at a basic annual\nsalary equal to or greater than the maximum salary of their salary\ngrade, as follows:\n\n*for those employees who have completed less than eight years, $2,250;\n\n*for those employees who have completed at least eight years but less\nthan 13 years, $4,600;\n\n*for those employees who have completed more than 13 years,\n$6,9001{1}.\n\n-Provides for the payment of pensionable annual location pay during\neach fiscal year for certain affected employees as follows:\n\n*for employees whose principal place of employment is in New York\nCity, Nassau County, Rockland County, Suffolk County or Westchester\nCounty, location pay of:\n\n- $3,697, for the fiscal year commencing April 1, 2017;\n\n- $4,000, for the fiscal year commencing April 1, 2018, except that\nsuch amount shall increase to $4,100, effective October 1, 2018;\n\n- $4,200, for the fiscal year commencing April 1, 2019 and each fiscal\nyear thereafter.\n\n*for employees whose principal place of employment is in Dutchess,\nPutnam or Orange County, location pay of:\n\n- $1,848, for the fiscal year commencing April 1, 2017;\n\n- 2,000, for the fiscal year commencing April 1, 2018, except that\nsuch amount shall increase to $2,050, effective October 1, 2018;\n\n- $2,100, for the fiscal year commencing April 1, 2019 and each fiscal\nyear thereafter.\n\n*for employees whose principal place of employment is in Monroe County\nand who were receiving location pay in 1985, location pay of:\n\n- $200 for the fiscal year commencing April 1, 2017 and for each\nfiscal year thereafter.\n\nWhere any of these employees already has received location pay during\nthe periods indicated pursuant to any other law, the amounts specified\nherein will be offset by the amounts received.\n\n-Provides that, for all employees, increments and partial increments\nshall not be paid unless an otherwise eligible employee shall have\nreceived other than an unsatisfactory performance rating for his or\nher services during the year immediately preceding (pursuant to a\nperformance evaluation system set forth by the Chief Administrative\nJudge, for unrepresented employees, or in the collective bargaining\nagreement between the parties, for represented employees).\n\n-In the fashion of past legislation implementing collective bargaining\nagreements between the Judiciary and its employees, provides that,\nwhere appropriate, the salary increases authorized in this measure\nshall be extended to unrepresented nonjudicial employees of the\ncourts.\n\nThis measure would take effect retroactively to April 1, 2017.\n\n 2017 LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nOCA 2017-74\nAssembly 8102 (M. of A. Weinstein) (referred to Judiciary)\n\n{1} These payments, initiated in 2016 (see L. 2014, c. 400), replace\nthe longevity and extra-longevity increments formerly provided on the\nsalary schedules on which graded nonjudicial officers and employees\naffected by this measure are placed.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
